---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Institutional Partners">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Institutional Partners</h1>
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/network">Network</a> / Institutional Partners</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="container">
      <p>
        The SCAN II project collaborates with national enforcement authorities, judicial bodies, and
        professional organizations across Europe to ensure our research and platform reflect real-world
        practice.
      </p>

      <h2>Types of Institutional Partners</h2>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>National Enforcement Authorities</h3>
          <p>Bailiffs, enforcement officers, and judicial enforcement bodies across EU Member States.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Judicial Bodies</h3>
          <p>Courts and judicial institutions involved in cross-border enforcement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Professional Organizations</h3>
          <p>Bar associations, chambers of enforcement officers, and legal professional bodies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>EU Institutions</h3>
          <p>European Commission and other EU bodies working on civil justice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Collaboration</h2>
      <p>
        Our institutional partners contribute to the project by:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Providing information on national enforcement procedures</li>
        <li>Validating research findings</li>
        <li>Participating in project events and workshops</li>
        <li>Disseminating project results to practitioners</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Become a Partner</h2>
      <p>
        If your organization is interested in collaborating with the SCAN II project, please contact us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
